# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0). GitHub shows a "Cite this repository" button from this file and
# Zenodo reads it when a release is archived. Add the Zenodo concept DOI under `identifiers` after the first release,
# and the journal article under `preferred-citation` once it is published.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the derived datasets, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "physiofire: satellite chlorophyll fluorescence (SIF/APAR), drought and fire-prone conditions in the Iberian Peninsula"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, configuration and derived datasets for the study "Drought sensitivity versus anticipation:
  satellite chlorophyll fluorescence and fire-prone conditions in the Iberian Peninsula": a matched comparison of
  burned and unburned cells before the large fires of 2025, the drought accumulation time scale of SIF/APAR, NDVI
  and EVI, and their response timing at drought onset, from TROPOMI SIF, MODIS, ERA5-Land and a daily SPEI at
  0.05 degrees for 2018-2025. Analysis plans and decision criteria were fixed before execution (git tags
  prereg-fire2025, prereg-timescale and prereg-onset).
authors:
  - family-names: Franquesa
    given-names: Magí
    affiliation: "Instituto Pirenaico de Ecología (IPE-CSIC), Zaragoza, Spain"
repository-code: "https://github.com/magifranquesa/physiofire"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-12"
keywords:
  - solar-induced chlorophyll fluorescence
  - TROPOMI
  - SIF/APAR
  - drought
  - SPEI
  - fire danger
  - Fire Weather Index
  - Iberian Peninsula
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24179252   # Zenodo concept DOI (resolves to the latest version)
    description: "Zenodo archive of the code (all versions)"
